1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,132
MeltWise: an AI energy copilot for India's induction-furnace foundries.

2
00:00:05,132 --> 00:00:11,015
This is our working prototype, for Phase 2 of the Yuva Yodha Energy Tech Hackathon.

3
00:00:11,915 --> 00:00:16,382
India's five thousand foundries waste fifty to eighty kilowatt-hours per

4
00:00:16,382 --> 00:00:20,787
tonne between melts in the same furnace, from operating practice alone.

5
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:23,145
Nobody sees it until the monthly bill.

6
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:26,743
MeltWise shows it while the metal is still in the furnace.

7
00:00:27,643 --> 00:00:32,430
Here is what we built. The furnace meter talks Modbus to an offline-first

8
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:37,085
edge gateway. A physics-informed model, a live advisor, a scheduler and

9
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:39,511
a carbon record run behind a web app.

10
00:00:39,511 --> 00:00:44,167
We have no plant yet, so a calibrated furnace simulator plays the plant

11
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:48,691
and the meter, and every result is measured against its ground truth.

12
00:00:49,991 --> 00:00:54,951
This melt is streaming live from the simulated Modbus meter, through the

13
00:00:54,951 --> 00:00:56,536
gateway, into MeltWise.

14
00:01:07,542 --> 00:01:12,312
Within two minutes, MeltWise spots under-powered melting, and tracks the

15
00:01:12,312 --> 00:01:15,691
energy used against a target for this exact charge.

16
00:01:19,606 --> 00:01:24,536
The red line is furnace power. The dashed line is MeltWise's live estimate

17
00:01:24,536 --> 00:01:27,800
of the bath temperature, from the energy balance.

18
00:01:49,422 --> 00:01:52,054
Now we cut the network for ten seconds.

19
00:01:52,054 --> 00:01:57,047
The gateway keeps every reading in a local outbox, and sends them all when

20
00:01:57,047 --> 00:01:59,544
the network returns. Nothing is lost.

21
00:02:15,271 --> 00:02:20,350
The bath is near target, so MeltWise asks for a temperature dip, and resets

22
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:22,246
its estimate on the reading.

23
00:02:22,546 --> 00:02:28,479
Target reached: tap now. Today, operators overshoot by about forty-two degrees.

24
00:02:28,479 --> 00:02:31,258
Following this prompt, by about five.

25
00:02:31,558 --> 00:02:36,408
The same prompts appear in the operator's own language: Hindi, and Tamil.

26
00:02:36,708 --> 00:02:41,849
If the metal has to wait for the moulds, MeltWise counts the cost of holding.

27
00:02:43,659 --> 00:02:46,734
The manager sees energy per tonne for every day:

28
00:02:46,734 --> 00:02:50,130
thirty days before MeltWise, and thirty days with it.

29
00:02:50,130 --> 00:02:52,693
And where the extra kilowatt-hours went.

30
00:02:53,593 --> 00:02:56,540
Any melt opens its power curve and breakdown.

31
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:01,452
This one used six hundred and sixty-seven kilowatt-hours per tonne, against

32
00:03:01,452 --> 00:03:04,858
six hundred and ten for best practice on its charge.

33
00:03:05,758 --> 00:03:10,102
The planner starts each heat so the metal is ready when the moulds are.

34
00:03:10,102 --> 00:03:13,956
Over three hundred simulated days, it cut holding time by half.

35
00:03:14,856 --> 00:03:19,263
And every batch gets a metered carbon record, which a buyer can download.

36
00:03:20,163 --> 00:03:22,909
We measured everything against ground truth.

37
00:03:22,909 --> 00:03:27,341
MeltWise predicts each melt's energy within one point four percent, and

38
00:03:27,341 --> 00:03:32,459
finds each practice cause with a correlation of point nine one to point nine nine.

39
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:38,487
In a simulated sixty-day pilot, with operators following sixty percent of

40
00:03:38,487 --> 00:03:43,403
prompts, energy per tonne fell by twenty-two point six kilowatt-hours:

41
00:03:43,403 --> 00:03:48,390
four point three lakh rupees, and thirty-eight tonnes of carbon dioxide

42
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:52,183
a year, for one furnace. These are simulation results.

43
00:03:52,183 --> 00:03:54,431
Next, we test on a real furnace.

44
00:03:55,331 --> 00:03:57,630
MeltWise. Every melt, measured.

45
00:03:57,630 --> 00:04:01,486
By Surianandhan Sridhar and Sameera Hussainy Pattan.

